diff --git a/docs/labwc-config.5.scd b/docs/labwc-config.5.scd
index cf142cf..cb83a35 100644
--- a/docs/labwc-config.5.scd
+++ b/docs/labwc-config.5.scd
@@ -1581,3 +1581,32 @@ See xkeyboard-config(7) for details.
 # SEE ALSO
 
 labwc(1), labwc-actions(5), labwc-theme(5)
+
+# AQUARIUS DECORATION COLORS
+
+*<windowRules><windowRule decorationColors="">*
+	Aquarius extension: six whitespace-separated opaque #RRGGBB colors, in
+	this order: active title background, inactive title background, active
+	border, inactive border, active title text, inactive title text.
+	The whole palette is selected by the last matching rule that specifies
+	this property. "default" restores the desktop theme, and so does an
+	invalid palette: a malformed value never inherits the palette of an
+	earlier, broader rule. Backgrounds are solid; dimensions and shadows continue to
+	follow the desktop theme, and so do the button images unless
+	decorationButtons is also given. Colors apply when decorations are
+	created, including after Reconfigure; title changes alone do not rematch.
+
+*<windowRules><windowRule decorationButtons="">*
+	Aquarius extension: the name of a folder INSIDE the theme directory
+	(<theme-dir>/<theme-name>/labwc/<folder>/) from which this window's
+	title-bar button images are loaded, so selected windows can carry buttons
+	drawn for their own frame colors. One plain path segment only: no slash,
+	no "..". The set is selected by the last matching rule that specifies
+	this property; "default" restores the theme's own buttons, and so does a
+	value this rule cannot use -- a malformed value never inherits a folder
+	named by an earlier, broader rule. Button names, states, geometry,
+	placement and hover behaviour are unchanged. Any picture the folder does
+	not provide -- including all of them, if the folder is missing -- stays
+	the theme's own picture, so a window can never end up with buttons the
+	rest of the desktop does not have. Applies when decorations are created,
+	including after Reconfigure.
